| **Content Security & CORS** | None added. | No explicit CORS rules; if this API is called from a browser, it could be misused via CSRF or data exfiltration. | Add `app.use(cors());` with a whitelist, or refuse all cross‑origin requests unless necessary. |
| **Input validation / sanitisation** | All endpoints use hard‑coded data; none accept user input. | In real apps, unvalidated user data can lead to XSS, injection, or logic flaws. | For every route that accepts body/query params, validate/sanitize them using a library (e.g., **Joi** or **express-validator**). |
